   "s": "City of Hollywood Code § 99.03(F): spearfishing is prohibited within <b>100 yards of the public/municipal beach</b>. The beach is defined as running from mean high water to 50 yards offshore, so the closure reaches <b>150 yards</b> from mean high water.",
   "src": "Seaward of the NOAA ENC coastline (harbour band, cells US5FL5RO and US5PEFBA, CC0), from where it leaves the City of Hallandale Beach (TIGERweb incorporated places) at 25.98699 N to the south boundary of Dr. Von D. Mizell-Eula Johnson State Park (FDEP) at 26.06053 N. Drawn at 175 yd, 50 yd of beach plus 125 per cent of the 100 yd, the margin the project uses for distance buffers.",
   "flag": "(1) TIGER puts the coast from 26.05486 N to 26.06053 N inside the City of Dania Beach (its beach park), not Hollywood; the ordinance's own words run to the state park, so that stretch is drawn, but Hollywood's ordinance may not reach it. (2) The chart coastline stands in for mean high water; on NAIP imagery elsewhere on this coast the chart line sits up to about 30 m landward of the waterline, which the 175 yd variant absorbs. (3) The ends are drawn perpendicular to the shore at the city line and the park line, not along the city boundary offshore."
